# Cliff₂ derives the decoded Selinger relations (Appendices A, F.1, G.1)

The derivations of Appendix A, each replayed line by line from the paper's
figures, then the decoding of every relation C1–C15 of Selinger's
presentation (Appendix G.1, `rel_derivable`) and the round trips of the
generators (Appendix F.1, `DE`).  Each step between two printed lines was
found by a search over rewrites modulo commuting gates on disjoint wires,
using the rules the paper cites for that step (and, where the paper applies
a rule in a derived form, its inverse or its image upside down), and is
replayed by `derive`.  Three steps the search does not reach in one go are
split by intermediate lines (`gen/cliff2.py`, `EXTRA`): two in
(3CNOTcontrolcommut), and the first step of the decoding of (C15), which
turns the decoded `CZ`'s round one at a time by (czrev).

Generated by `gen/gen_cliff.py` from the derivations `gen/run_cliffd.py`
finds (the figures read by `gen/figparse.py`).
-/
